:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-D7\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\" transform=\"translate(778,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mfrac\"><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(220,394) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"31\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-31\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(220,-345) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"32\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-32\"></use></g><rect width=\"553.6\" height=\"60\" x=\"120\" y=\"220\"></rect></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(1849.3,0)\"><use data-c=\"3D\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-3D\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(2905.1,0)\"><use data-c=\"33\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-33\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>.</p>\n<p>Number of octahedral voids = 4.</p>\n<p>Number of tetrahedral voids = 8.</p>\n<p>Therefore, per atom, there is one octahedral void and two tetrahedral voids.</p>\n<p>In fcc (or ccp), the unit edge length is given by</p>\n<p><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -1.334ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"28.55ex\" height=\"3.507ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -960.5 12618.9 1550\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"msqrt\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(0,100.5)\"><use data-c=\"221A\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-221A\"></use></g><g transform=\"translate(853,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mn\"><use data-c=\"32\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-32\"></use></g></g><rect width=\"500\" height=\"60\" x=\"853\" y=\"840.5\"></rect></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(1353,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D44E\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D44E\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(2159.8,0)\"><use data-c=\"3D\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-3D\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(